      - “Embedded” PV (≥1 PM and ≥1 PF neighbor): 681 cells.
      - “Isolated” PV (no PM and no PF neighbors): 461 cells.
    - DE (embedded vs isolated PV; FDR<0.05): 169 genes upregulated in embedded PV.
      - Top up genes include ABCC9, ADGRL1, ADM, AGPS, ALDH1A2, ANGPT1, APOE, ARHGAP18, ARHGAP29, ARL6IP1.
    - Within a coarse signaling/stress-related set (e.g. CXCL/BMP/FGF/PDGF/VEGF/NOTCH, and AGT, ANGPT1, ADM), 6 genes are significantly upregulated in embedded PV, including ADM, ANGPT1, FGF12, NOTCH1, PDGFRA, PDGFRB.
    - The size of the embedded-up module (169 genes) plus specific signaling-related factors supports a distinct community-associated PV program when PV cells are in PV–PM–PF micro-environments.
  - Quality (0–10): Derivable=7, Novel=6, Feasible=8, Specific=8, Falsifiable=9.

